<title>GERMANY: Waigel says Germany won't sell gold for EMU.</title>
<headline>Waigel says Germany won't sell gold for EMU.</headline>
<dateline>BONN 1997-04-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Finance Minister Theo Waigel said on Wednesday Germany had no plans to sell gold to meet the fiscal criteria for European monetary union.</p>
<p>&quot;We will not sell gold,&quot; Waigel told parliament's finance committee.</p>
<p>German officials including Chancellor Helmut Kohl and Bundesbank president Hans Tietmeyer have repeatedly said they oppose gold sales by central banks and the International Monetary Fund to meet budget needs.</p>
<p>Economic growth will help Germany bring its budget deficit in line with the EMU targets, Waigel said.</p>
<p>-- Bonn Newsroom, 49-228-26097150</p>
</text>
